<title>SWEDEN: Goldman denies downgraded Nokia.</title>
<headline>Goldman denies downgraded Nokia.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Richard Kramer, analyst at Goldman Sachs in London, on Thursday denied a market rumour that he had downgraded his recommendation on Finnish telecommunications group Nokia Oy.</p>
<p>&quot;The recommendation has not been changed,&quot; Kramer told Reuters, adding that Goldman had Nokia as &quot;outperform&quot;. Stockholm market sources said the share came under late pressure on rumours Goldman had downgraded it.</p>
<p>Nokia closed Helsinki trade down four markka at 319.00, and in New York at 1535 GMT its ADR was down $2-7/8 at $64-1/4, the equivalent of 320.50 markka.</p>
<p>-- Henrik Persson +46 8 8-700 1011</p>
</text>
